  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1143 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nRain chances will increase on Saturday, as an upper trough moves\nthrough the Southwest US, and then closes off across the Southern\nRockies and Northern Mexico. Some divergence aloft, along with \nsome lift up and over the old frontal boundary should lead to \nincreased cloud cover Friday night into Saturday morning and the \neventually shower development into Saturday Night and Sunday \nmorning. CAMs still have their differences at this range, but \ngeneral idea of showers becoming more widespread Saturday evening \nacross the area and then maybe mixing in a little thunder Saturday\nnight into Sunday morning as the better lift moves into the area \nlooks on target. \n\nModel blends are showing highs in the low 60s on Saturday across\nthe area, but latest data coming in keeps readings in the 50s\nduring the day as the cloud cover develops. Will give it another\nrun or two to make sure its a real trend and the timing maintains\nbefore lowering highs, but would not surprise me if highs need to\nbe lowered some.\n\nSystem moves out late Sunday and a weak upper ridge builds into\nthe area. Dry and warmer as less cloud cover means more sunshine.\nHighs back in the 70s.",
